<Layout title="About" description="Who makes World Wide Hype, how posts are written and sourced, and how errors are corrected." pubDate={new Date('2026-10-14')}>
	<p>World Wide Hype explains major global stories (politics, economics, conflict, climate, technology and society) twice a day, at 00:00 and 07:00 UTC. Each post covers one story: what happened, the background, why it matters and what to watch next.</p>

	<p>One more thing: read every story on the home page map all the way to the end, and something extraordinary happens.</p>

	<h2>Who runs it</h2>
	<p>The site is run by a frontend developer (<a href="mailto:edik.choi@gmail.com">edik.choi@gmail.com</a>) in South Korea as an independent project. It is supported by display ads (Google AdSense) and has no sponsors or political affiliation. Advertisers have no say in which stories are covered or how.</p>

	<h2>How posts are made</h2>
	<p>Every post is researched and written by AI (Anthropic's Claude) following a fixed editorial process:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Stories are chosen from the previous 24 to 48 hours, rotating across topics and regions.</li>
		<li>Every fact is checked against at least two reputable sources, such as Reuters, AP, BBC, Al Jazeera, or government and international-organization releases. Anything that cannot be verified is left out or explicitly attributed.</li>
		<li>Numbers, dates and names are copied exactly as the sources give them.</li>
		<li>Infographics are drawn for each post using only figures from its cited sources.</li>
		<li>The tone is neutral and explanatory: no partisan opinion, no unsupported speculation.</li>
		<li>Analysis is kept to a clearly labelled Editor's Insight section near the end, built only on the facts and sources in the post.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>The sources used for every post are listed at the end of it, so you can read the original reporting.</p>

	<h2>Corrections</h2>
	<p>AI can make mistakes. Every post lists its sources so readers can check the original reporting, and confirmed errors are corrected in the post.</p>
</Layout>
